<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-cefa1.6 — schema type-hygiene pass, Tier B, P5 (epic nexus-cefa1;
    plan of record T2 nexus/plan-schema-type-hygiene-2026-08-12 [22360]).
    Template: telemetry-004-type-hygiene.xml (nexus-cefa1.3, P2) — the
    closest sibling for a DROP DEFAULT -> TYPE ... USING -> SET DEFAULT
    bracket shape on a NOT NULL DEFAULT column (there applied to boolean;
    here to jsonb), because unlike plans-002's plan_json (nexus-cefa1.5, P4,
    NOT NULL with NO default) topic_links.link_types carries a literal
    DEFAULT '[]' (taxonomy-001-baseline.xml:135) that must be dropped before
    the TYPE change and re-set afterward in the new type's own syntax.

    Retires the LAST still-TEXT Tier-B column of the arc: topic_links.
    link_types TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]' -> jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    in ONE changeset (ONE ALTER TABLE, one table rewrite):

ALTER TABLE nexus.topic_links
    ALTER COLUMN link_types DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN link_types TYPE jsonb USING link_types::jsonb,
    ALTER COLUMN link_types SET DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb;

    The USING clause is a PLAIN cast (link_types::jsonb, no NULLIF) — NOT
    NULL is preserved automatically across ALTER COLUMN TYPE (never
    touched), and the P0 pre-flight found empty_string_count=0 on the only
    populated deployment (see Data-safety evidence below), so there is no
    '' value that a NULLIF step would need to catch; a plain ::jsonb cast on
    an empty string would abort the ALTER with "invalid input syntax for
    type json" — this column is safe without a NULLIF guard because that
    value never occurs, confirmed by the count, not assumed (identical
    reasoning to plans-002-jsonb.xml's plan_json branch, which is also NOT
    NULL with a plain cast).

    ALTER COLUMN TYPE is ordinary DDL (an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE table rewrite),
    not RLS-filtered DML — no FORCE RLS toggle needed, and the changeset
    touches no row via INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.

    Data-safety evidence: T2 nexus/schema-hygiene-p0-preflight-2026-08-15
    [22588] (nexus-cefa1.1), cloud (the only populated deployment; this
    box's local substrate is a fresh hermetic pytest engine with no seeded
    data): topic_links.link_types total_rows=9749, null_count=0,
    empty_string_count=0, invalid_cast_count=0 — every row already holds
    valid JSON, confirming the plain ::jsonb cast above is safe on live
    data, not merely reasoned from the writers.

    Consumer audit (nexus-cefa1.6, mirroring nexus-cefa1.2/.3/.4/.5's
    sweeps): swept every Java and Python write/read path touching
    topic_links.link_types.
    - Java writes: TaxonomyRepository.upsertTopicLink (live-compute,
      EXCLUDED-overwrite conflict policy), .importTopicLink (ETL,
      GREATEST-on-count conflict policy), the private static
      importLinksBatch (multi-row ETL import), .generateCooccurrenceLinks
      (hardcoded "[\"cooccurrence\"]" literal), and .refreshProjectionLinks
      (the one path with real merge logic, see below) all now route the
      Java String through JsonbSupport.jsonbRequired (link_types is NOT
      NULL, same shape as plans.plan_json — the required-field variant, not
      jsonbOrNull) before binding it as the jOOQ-generated JSONB field type;
      every hand-built `field("EXCLUDED.link_types", ...)` conflict-target
      fragment is retyped from String.class to JSONB.class to match.
    - Java reads: refreshProjectionLinks SELECTs TOPIC_LINKS.LINK_TYPES to
      decide whether an existing link pair already carries the
      "projection" type; the fetched value is now a JSONB, unwrapped via
      .data() to recover the raw JSON-array text before the SAME crude
      substring-merge algorithm as before (`.contains("\"projection\"")`,
      then a bracket-replace to splice the new type into the array) runs
      UNCHANGED — this changeset does not alter that algorithm's behaviour
      in any way, only the plumbing that gets a Java String in and a JSONB
      out. Postgres's jsonb canonicalization only reorders/reformats OBJECT
      keys; JSON ARRAY element order (what link_types is) is preserved
      verbatim, so the substring check and the bracket-splice both continue
      to see the same array contents they always did, merely re-spaced.
    - getTopicLinkPairs never selects LINK_TYPES at all (only
      FROM_TOPIC_ID/TO_TOPIC_ID/LINK_COUNT) — no read-side change there.
    - Python: src/nexus/db/t2/http_taxonomy_store.py's upsert_topic_links
      and import_topic_link always `json.dumps(...)` before sending over
      the wire (never a bare unquoted string); getTopicLinkPairs's HTTP
      response never includes link_types, so no Python reader ever parses
      it back. The retired taxonomy_etl.py (RDR-158 SQLite retirement) is
      the only historical writer that shaped link_types payloads for the
      ETL import path; it no longer exists in src/nexus (grepped — only a
      stale __pycache__/*.pyc remains). No text-equality, hash, or dedup
      consumer of link_types exists in either language; the topic_links
      identity is the (tenant_id, from_topic_id, to_topic_id) primary key,
      never link_types content.
    - Test literals: a handful of TaxonomyRepositoryTest.java call sites
      passed BARE, non-JSON-encoded strings ("projection", "co-occurrence",
      "co-occur") straight through upsertTopicLink/importTopicLink/
      importBatch("link", ...) — tolerated only because the column was
      untyped TEXT with no server-side JSON validation. A plain ::jsonb
      column rejects those literals outright (unquoted bareword is not
      valid JSON), so every such literal is updated to a valid JSON array
      (e.g. "[\"co-occur\"]") in the corresponding Java test changes; this
      was always incidental to TEXT typing, never a real production shape
      (every production writer already emitted a JSON-encoded array).

    Handler-side validation (nexus-cefa1.6): TaxonomyHandler.handleUpsertLink,
    .handleImportLink, and the "link" branch of .handleImportBatch's per-row
    loop now validate an optional, present link_types value with the shared
    HttpUtil.rejectMalformedJson helper (AspectHandler/PlanHandler's
    extraction, nexus-cefa1.4/.5) — malformed JSON 400s at the handler,
    naming rows[i] in the batch path; class-22 SQLSTATE 422
    (HttpUtil.sendTypedDbError) remains the backstop for any write path
    that bypasses the handler (e.g. a direct repository call).

    ANALYZE after the rewrite (BUG-0148 invariant, rdr180-16-analyze-
    rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically enforced by
    tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py) — the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE above
    resets nexus.topic_links's planner statistics.

    Rollback: mirrors telemetry-004's is_batch rollback shape (a NOT NULL
    DEFAULT column) applied to jsonb-to-TEXT instead of boolean-to-INTEGER —
    DROP DEFAULT -> TYPE TEXT USING link_types::text -> SET DEFAULT '[]',
    restoring the exact pre-migration TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]' shape
    (taxonomy-001-baseline.xml:135).

    Ordering: registered after plans-002-jsonb.xml (P4) and before the
    grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block, NOT back in the taxonomy-00N
    family's own section near the top of the changelog — matches the
    master changelog's established convention for every new changeset
    since RDR-156 (catalog-031, telemetry-004, aspects-003, plans-002 all
    append near the current tail rather than splicing back into their
    family's original block; see those files' own <include> comments in
    db.changelog-master.xml for the identical reasoning). This is the FINAL
    phase of the schema type-hygiene arc (epic nexus-cefa1) — after this
    changeset ships, all 10 audited columns (4 Tier A timestamp/boolean, 6
    Tier B jsonb) are converted; nexus-cefa1.7 runs the arc's final gate.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset taxonomy-008-1-link-types-jsonb ───────────────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="taxonomy-008-1-link-types-jsonb" author="nexus-cefa1.6">
        <comment>
            topic_links.link_types TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]' -> jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT
            '[]'::jsonb (DROP DEFAULT -> TYPE ... USING plain cast -> SET DEFAULT).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.topic_links
    ALTER COLUMN link_types DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN link_types TYPE jsonb USING link_types::jsonb,
    ALTER COLUMN link_types SET DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb;

-- BUG-0148 invariant (rdr180-16-analyze-rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically
-- enforced by tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py): the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE
-- above rewrites nexus.topic_links and resets its planner statistics.
ANALYZE nexus.topic_links;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
ALTER TABLE nexus.topic_links
    ALTER COLUMN link_types DROP DEFAULT,
    ALTER COLUMN link_types TYPE TEXT USING link_types::text,
    ALTER COLUMN link_types SET DEFAULT '[]';

ANALYZE nexus.topic_links;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
